              with links to the manual pages at tag 6.0.0. The manual itself is
              not bundled. One topic per module family: the 3.0.0 topics kept
              their names, parser_markup (Html, Svg, MathML, Markup) and
              parser_streaming (decoders and encoders, QIF, OFX) are new in 6.0.0
verify/    <- ours: every snippet on overview.md, in one app
overview.md <- ours: the page get_roc_syntax(topic: "roc-parser") returns

# Mapping notes, 3.0.0 -> 6.0.0 (the APIs the topics teach):
#   Utf8, Literal              -> Parser.Utf8, Parser.Quotation (not modules of
#                                 their own; `import parser.Utf8` is an error)
#   Utf8.parse_str(p, text)    -> p.parse_str(text); parse_str_partial -> run_str
#   Parser(input, a)           -> Parser(input, a, problem); primitives without
#                                 an argument are factories: digits({})
#   ParseError({ message, offset }) and every format's { line, column, message }
#                              -> Parser.Diagnostic(problem): { problem, location, path }
#   CSV.parse / parse_normalized / parse_headerless
#                              -> CSV.decode_str(text, { header: Exact | Normalized | Absent })
#   MissingRequiredField(Str) as its own tag -> a problem inside InvalidCsv / InvalidYaml
#   CSV.parse_records / parse_with / decode -> CSV.parse_str(...).records,
#                                 CSV.rows_parser({ row }), document.decode_rows
#   Yaml.decode / Yaml.decoder(opts) -> Yaml.decode_str(text, { keys, unknown_keys })
#   JsonValue.parse_with / to_str -> JsonValue.parse_str(text, props) / value.encode(props) (bytes)
#   AsciiDoc.render / parse_with / select_include_with
#                              -> document.render_html() / parse_str(text, props) /
#                                 select_include(source, attributes, { tabsize })
#   RocSyntax.parse_expr_str   -> RocSyntax.parse_str(text, { mode: Expression })
#   HTTP.parse_request / parse_response / header / request
#                              -> HTTP.Request.parse_bytes / HTTP.Response.parse_bytes /
#                                 request.header(name) / HTTP.Request.parser({})
#   HTTP.RequestLiteral        -> a literal annotated HTTP.Request
#   new: Html, Svg, MathML, Markup, QIF, OFX, Xml.Namespaced, Xml.reader, and
#        decoder/encoder receivers (read_iter, read_stream, write_stream)
